<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">

<head>
  <%- include("../../components/seo-head", {
    title: "Privacy Policy — DevHub",
    description: "How DevHub collects, uses, stores, and protects your personal information. Written in plain English with no legal jargon.",
    canonicalPath: "/privacy",
    keywords: "DevHub privacy, privacy policy, data protection, GDPR, user data",
    ogType: "website",
    extraStyles: ["/styles/legal.css"]
  }) %>
</head>

<body>
  <%- include("../../components/header") %>

  <main class="legal-page">

    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <header class="legal-hero">
      <div class="legal-hero__inner">
        <span class="legal-hero__badge">Legal</span>
        <h1 class="legal-hero__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-hero__sub">
          How DevHub collects, uses, and protects your information.
          Written in plain English — no walls of legal jargon.
        </p>
        <p class="legal-hero__updated">
          <strong>Last updated:</strong> <time datetime="2026-01-01">January 1, 2026</time>
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ============ NOTICE ============ -->
    <div class="legal-notice" role="note">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
        <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
        <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8"></line>
      </svg>
      <p>
        This document is provided as a starting point for informational
        purposes and does not constitute legal advice. Consult a qualified
        attorney to adapt it to your jurisdiction and business model.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ TABLE OF CONTENTS ============ -->
    <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <h2 class="legal-toc__title">Contents</h2>
      <ol class="legal-toc__list">
        <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
        <li><a href="#data-we-collect">Data we collect</a></li>
        <li><a href="#how-we-use">How we use your data</a></li>
        <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies and tracking</a></li>
        <li><a href="#third-parties">Third-party services</a></li>
        <li><a href="#data-retention">Data retention</a></li>
        <li><a href="#your-rights">Your rights</a></li>
        <li><a href="#security">Security</a></li>
        <li><a href="#children">Children's privacy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#international">International transfers</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- ============ CONTENT ============ -->
    <article class="legal-content">

      <section id="overview" class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          DevHub is a community platform for discovering, reviewing, and
          sharing open-source projects. This Privacy Policy explains what
          information we collect when you use the platform, how we use
          it, and the choices available to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          We aim to collect only what is necessary to operate the service,
          to be transparent about how that information is handled, and to
          give you meaningful control over your data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="data-we-collect" class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>

        <h3>2.1 Information you provide</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Account data</strong> — your display name, username,
            email address, and password hash (never the plain-text password).</li>
          <li><strong>Profile data</strong> — your avatar, biography, and any
            other fields you choose to fill in.</li>
          <li><strong>Content you publish</strong> — projects, screenshots,
            demo videos, downloadable files, reviews, ratings, and comments.</li>
          <li><strong>Support tickets</strong> — the name, email address,
            subject, category, and message you submit through the contact form.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.2 Information collected automatically</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Session data</strong> — an identifier, the login
            timestamp, the last activity timestamp, and a short device
            fingerprint used to help you manage active sessions.</li>
          <li><strong>Network data</strong> — your IP address and user agent
            string, recorded on each session for security and abuse prevention.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage data</strong> — view counts, download counts, and
            aggregated interaction statistics that help us rank and display
            projects.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.3 Information from third parties</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong> — when you link a repository to a
            project, we retrieve public metadata such as stars, forks,
            language, license, and release download counts. We do not
            retrieve private repository contents unless you explicitly
            link a private repository and authorize it.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="how-we-use" class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. How we use your data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To create and secure your account, and to authenticate you.</li>
          <li>To display your profile and published content to other users,
            consistent with your visibility settings.</li>
          <li>To operate features such as reviews, comments, and ticket
            handling.</li>
          <li>To synchronize public repository metadata from GitHub.</li>
          <li>To detect abuse, enforce rate limits, and prevent fraud.</li>
          <li>To send transactional email — such as verification codes and
            password reset links — when required.</li>
          <li>To measure aggregate usage and improve the service.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use your
          content to train third-party advertising models.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies" class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          DevHub uses a small number of strictly necessary cookies:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Session cookies</strong> — <code>access_token</code> and
            <code>refresh_token</code>, both HTTP-only and Secure in
            production. These are required for authentication and session
            management.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Preference storage</strong> — the theme and accent
            choices you make are stored locally in your browser using
            <code>localStorage</code>. These never leave your device.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use advertising cookies, cross-site tracking pixels, or
          third-party analytics that profile you across the web.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="third-parties" class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>

        <h3>5.1 GitHub</h3>
        <p>
          Project metadata is retrieved from the public GitHub API. Requests
          are made from our servers and may include the repository owner and
          name. GitHub's own privacy policy governs data processed on their
          side.
        </p>

        <h3>5.2 Email delivery</h3>
        <p>
          Transactional email is delivered through an SMTP provider. The
          recipient address and message content are transmitted to that
          provider solely for delivery purposes.
        </p>

        <h3>5.3 Hosting and infrastructure</h3>
        <p>
          The service runs on cloud infrastructure. Application logs,
          database records, and uploaded files are stored on infrastructure
          we control and are accessible only to authorized operators.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="data-retention" class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Active accounts</strong> — retained for as long as
            your account remains open.</li>
          <li><strong>Deleted accounts</strong> — content associated with a
            deleted account is removed within 30 days, except where we are
            legally required to retain it or where it has been aggregated
            into anonymized statistics.</li>
          <li><strong>Session records</strong> — expired or revoked sessions
            are purged automatically.</li>
          <li><strong>Support tickets</strong> — retained for up to 24 months
            after resolution, for reference and audit purposes.</li>
          <li><strong>Application logs</strong> — retained for up to 90 days.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="your-rights" class="legal-section">
        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have some or all of the
          following rights:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal data
            we hold about you.</li>
          <li><strong>Correction</strong> — update or fix inaccurate
            information from your account settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Deletion</strong> — request that your account and its
            associated content be removed.</li>
          <li><strong>Export</strong> — receive your data in a portable
            format.</li>
          <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to specific processing
            activities, such as analytics.</li>
          <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent</strong> — where processing is
            based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details at
          the end of this document. We respond to verifiable requests within
          30 days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="security" class="legal-section">
        <h2>8. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to
          protect your information, including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Passwords hashed with a modern, memory-hard algorithm.</li>
          <li>HTTP-only, Secure, SameSite cookies for session tokens.</li>
          <li>Rate limiting on authentication and sensitive endpoints.</li>
          <li>Least-privilege access controls for administrative tools.</li>
          <li>Regular dependency updates and security advisories.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          No system is completely secure. If you discover a vulnerability,
          please see <code>SECURITY.md</code> in the project repository for
          responsible disclosure instructions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="children" class="legal-section">
        <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          DevHub is not directed at children under 13, and we do not
          knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a
          child has provided us with personal information, contact us so we
          can remove it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="international" class="legal-section">
        <h2>10. International transfers</h2>
        <p>
          DevHub is operated from servers that may be located outside your
          country of residence. By using the service, you acknowledge that
          your information may be transferred to, stored in, and processed
          in jurisdictions whose data protection laws may differ from yours.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes" class="legal-section">
        <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do,
          we update the "Last updated" date at the top of the page. Material
          changes will be announced in-product or by email at least 14 days
          before taking effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="legal-section">
        <h2>12. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy can be submitted through our contact
          form, which creates a tracked support ticket:
        </p>
        <div class="legal-cta">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Contact Us</a>
          <a href="/legal/terms" class="btn-outline">Terms of Service</a>
        </div>
        <p>
          You can also reach the maintainers through the project repository
          on GitHub.
        </p>
      </section>

    </article>

    <!-- ============ FOOTER NAV ============ -->
    <div class="legal-footer">
      <a href="/legal/privacy" class="legal-footer__link legal-footer__link--active">Privacy Policy</a>
      <span class="legal-footer__sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/legal/terms" class="legal-footer__link">Terms of Service</a>
      <span class="legal-footer__sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/contact" class="legal-footer__link">Contact</a>
    </div>

  </main>

  <%- include("../../components/footer") %>
</body>

</html>